Using the chain rule:
$$\begin{align*}
\frac{d}{dx}[f(2x)] &= 2f'(2x) \\
2f'(2x) &= x^2 \\
f'(2x) &= \frac{x^2}{2}
\end{align*}$$
Let $u=2x$, so $x=\frac{u}{2}$.
$$\begin{align*}
f'(u) &= \frac{\left(\frac{u}{2}\right)^2}{2} \\
&= \frac{u^2}{8}
\end{align*}$$
Therefore:
$$\begin{align*}
f'(x) &= \frac{x^2}{8}
\end{align*}$$

